# Third-party clones — disposable, never committed (and unlicensed data stays out of our repo)
external/

# Generated data and model outputs (release-as-data-bus later if needed)
output/
# ONE EXCEPTION, added 2026-09-14. This is 278 bytes of FITTED CONSTANTS, not
# data: five per-class sitting-member slopes. fit_seats_full.R hard-stops
# without it whenever AUSPOL_MP_SLOPE=1, which is the published default, and
# the file is produced by scripts/fit_mp_slope.R, which needs
# output/candidacies.csv, which needs build_candidacies.R, which needs
# external/reference/ directories CI never populates. That deadlock took the
# nightly Forecast refresh down for six consecutive runs (2026-09-10 to 09-14)
# and it was found only by opening the Actions tab.
#
# Tracking it lets the monitor run the REAL published configuration rather
# than a variant of it -- the alternative (AUSPOL_MP_SLOPE=0 in the workflow)
# would have the nightly job report numbers for a model that is not the one
# that ships, which defeats the point of the job.
#
# REFIT IT when output/candidacies.csv changes: Rscript scripts/fit_mp_slope.R.
# Provenance for the committed copy is in docs/CONSTANTS.md. Remove this
# exception once build_candidacies.R can run in CI -- that is the real fix and
# is already queued (NEWS 0.4.34).
!output/
output/*
!output/mp-slope-by-class.csv
*.parquet
*.rds

# R
.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
.RData
*.Rcheck/

# OS
Thumbs.db

# compiled objects from src/ (devtools::load_all)
src/*.o
src/*.dll
src/*.so
src/*.o-*
